/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 604.50 Tm (1. `Rover.cpp` gets the active HAL with `AP_HAL::get_HAL\(\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 593.00 Tm (2. In a Linux build, `AP_HAL::get_HAL\(\)` returns the global `HAL_Linux hal_linux`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 581.50 Tm (3. `HAL_Linux` passes a `Linux::Scheduler` object into the generic `AP_HAL::HAL` base ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 570.00 Tm (class.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 558.50 Tm (4. The base HAL stores that object as `hal.scheduler`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 547.00 Tm (5. `AP_HAL_MAIN_CALLBACKS\(&rover\)` creates `main\(\)` and calls `hal.run\(argc, argv, ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 535.50 Tm (&rover\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 524.00 Tm (6. Because `hal` is actually `HAL_Linux`, this calls `HAL_Linux::run\(\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 512.50 Tm (7. `HAL_Linux::run\(\)` starts the Linux platform scheduler and repeatedly calls the ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 501.00 Tm (vehicle callback loop.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 489.50 Tm (8. The vehicle callback loop is `AP_Vehicle::loop\(\)`, not `Rover::loop\(\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 478.00 Tm (9. `AP_Vehicle::loop\(\)` calls `AP_Scheduler::loop\(\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 466.50 Tm (10. `AP_Scheduler::loop\(\)` runs tasks from `Rover::scheduler_tasks[]`.) Tj
