BT
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 800.00 Tm ( direct include. In a Linux build, `AP_HAL::get_HAL\(\)` returns `hal_linux`; ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 788.50 Tm (`HAL_Linux` installs `Linux::Scheduler` as `hal.scheduler`; and `HAL_Linux::run\(\)` ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 777.00 Tm (starts that platform scheduler.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 765.50 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 754.00 Tm (There is no `Rover::loop\(\)` implementation in `Rover.cpp`. `Rover` inherits from ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 742.50 Tm (`AP_Vehicle`, and `AP_Vehicle` implements the final HAL callback `loop\(\)`.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 731.00 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 719.50 Tm (The real `callbacks` pointer in `HAL_Linux::run\(\)` is `&rover`. Its static type is ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 708.00 Tm (`AP_HAL::HAL::Callbacks*`, but the actual object is the global `Rover rover`. Calling ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 696.50 Tm (`callbacks->setup\(\)` and `callbacks->loop\(\)` invokes `AP_Vehicle::setup\(\)` and ) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 685.00 Tm (`AP_Vehicle::loop\(\)` on that Rover object.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 673.50 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 662.00 Tm (The final runtime picture is:) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 650.50 Tm () Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 639.00 Tm () Tj
/F3 7.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 634.00 Tm (Linux::Scheduler) Tj
/F3 7.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 625.30 Tm (  supports HAL/platform timing, delays, threads, IO, UART, RC input, and failsafe callbacks.) Tj
/F3 7.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 616.60 Tm () Tj
/F3 7.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 605.10 Tm (AP_Scheduler) Tj
/F3 7.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 596.40 Tm (  runs Rover::scheduler_tasks[] and decides when Rover vehicle functions execute.) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 42 587.70 Tm () Tj
